repository-code: "https://github.com/kevinmneal/six-triangle-packing"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  An exact computer-assisted proof that the smallest equilateral triangle
  containing six unit equilateral triangles with pairwise disjoint interiors
  has side length (13+3 sqrt(13))/8, allowing independent rotations and legal
  boundary contact. The proof combines analytic reductions with a complete
  exact finite certificate. The construction is attributed to Maurizio
  Morandi through Erich Friedman's catalogue. This preprint has not been
  peer reviewed and is not a proof-kernel formalization.
keywords:
  - geometric packing
  - equilateral triangles
  - computer-assisted proof
  - exact certificates
